ernment headed the council  for six months this rotation was  dizzying and impeded proper monitoring  and execution of all the dossiers and I  were the fixed president the preparation  of European summits has become more  efficient if  if the rotating six-month country  presidencies haven't disappeared  concretely what does the president do  essentially he's three F's fixer of  meetings finder of compromise and  facilitator of consensus after each  summit the European Council president  goes to the European Parliament to  present the conclusions that have been  adopted is then grilled by any piece  abroad the president represents the  European Union a big set piece events  like the g7 and g20 along with the  president of the Commission as to  whether Europe should develop a  dedicated president of Europe roll  president who represents both the  European Commission and the Member  States well an idea does surface  regularly but it's not going to happen  anytime soon
 

